@startuml lens_lookup_sequence_diagram
title User Lens — persistent de-elevated agent (pick a person, see their devices)

actor Operator as OP
participant "FinderPresenter\n(coordinator)" as P
participant "PersonLensViewModel\n(detail pane)" as VM
participant "LensLookupWorker.ps1\n(pool, as admin)" as PW
participant "Scheduled Task\n(interactive user, Limited)" as TASK
participant "LensAgent.ps1\n(persistent, regular user)" as AG
participant "AD (Global Catalog)\n+ home domains" as AD
participant "SCCM AdminService\n(REST)" as SCCM

== App startup: warm the agent (parallel with DONUT boot) ==
P -> PW : BeginInvoke(-WarmOnly)  on the runspace pool
activate PW
note right of PW
  DONUT runs elevated as the admin account, which cannot read SCCM/BitLocker.
  So the lookup must run as the interactive (regular) user - once, persistently.
end note
PW -> PW : EnsureAgent (mutex): find the interactive user,\nlock the %ProgramData%\\DONUT\\lens-agent ACL\n(SYSTEM / Administrators / interactive user),\nmint the session AES key (key.bin)
PW -> TASK : register + start the task\n(conhost --headless so no console flashes)
activate TASK
TASK -> AG : run LensAgent.ps1 -ExchangeDir -ParentPid -SiteServer
deactivate TASK
activate AG
AG -> AG : write heartbeat, then pre-warm on a THREAD JOB\n(GC + domain binds, AdminService affinity + hardware\nroutes) so the serve loop starts serving at once
PW --> P : '' (agent ready) — reaped on first pick
deactivate PW
note over AG : agent idle; the SERVE LOOP beats every ~2s and\nnever blocks (a fresh beat proves it serves), exits when\nParentPid dies / stop.flag appears / dir purged

== Pick a user in the AD finder ==
OP -> P : click a USER row  (OnPickUser)
activate P
P -> VM : SetLoading(displayName); DetailMode = 'Person'
P -> PW : BeginInvoke(Identity, Sam, SiteServer)  on the pool
deactivate P
activate PW
PW -> PW : EnsureAgent (already warm -> no-op)
PW -> AG : write request-<id>.bin (AES, atomic)
activate AG

== Gather (as the regular user) ==
AG ->> SCCM : affinity on a THREAD JOB at t=0 (the Sam hint):\nendswith(UniqueUserName,'<SAM>') - the ONLY SCCM call\n(the /wmi route 404s richer filters)
AG -> AD : GC-locate the user (forest-wide) -> bind home domain\n(parallel with the affinity job)
AD --> AG : UPN / SAM / email / manager / office
AG -> AG : write partial-<id>-1.bin (directory facts)
SCCM --> AG : ResourceName(s)  (exact-tail filtered)
AG -> AG : write partial-<id>-2.bin (name-only device rows)
loop each WSID
  AG -> AD : GC-locate the computer -> OS + lastLogonTimestamp\n+ msFVE-RecoveryInformation (BitLocker)
end
AG -> AG : write result-<id>.bin (AES, atomic)
deactivate AG
note over AG : stays alive for the next pick

== Return + render ==
PW -> P : partials (100ms poll): decrypt partial-<id>-N.bin ->\nInformation stream 'LensPartial' -> ApplyPartial\n(person info, then device names, while details load)
PW -> PW : decrypt result-<id>.bin, delete this lookup's files
PW --> P : JSON bundle
deactivate PW
activate P
P -> P : PollLens: PersonLens.FromJson(json)
P -> VM : Apply(lens)  (person fields + LensDeviceViewModels)
P -> VM : wire each device's Reveal / Add command
P -> P : cache the bundle in memory (15-min TTL;\nre-picks render instantly, dies with the app)
deactivate P

== Act on a device ==
OP -> VM : click "Add" on a device
VM -> P : OnAddDeviceToList(wsid)
activate P
P -> P : EnsureRow + PrefetchIp + StartInventory + MoveRowToTop
P -> OP : machine added to the list (toast); Lens stays open
deactivate P

== Machine-owner batch (-OwnerOf) ==
P -> PW : BeginInvoke(-OwnerOf machines)  on the pool
activate PW
PW -> AG : write request-<id>.bin (kind = 'owner',\nthe whole machine list in ONE request)
activate AG
AG -> SCCM : Resolve-MachineOwnerBatch (primary users)
SCCM --> AG : owner per machine
AG -> AG : write result-<id>.bin — answered on a THREAD JOB\nlike person lookups, no partials
deactivate AG
PW --> P : owners bundle (machine -> owner)
deactivate PW

== App close ==
P -> PW : BeginInvoke(-StopAgent)  on the pool
activate PW
PW -> AG : StopAndPurgeAgent(): drop stop.flag,\nStop/Unregister the task, purge lens-* dirs
deactivate PW
@enduml
